#{[17592186278079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278079 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278079 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278079 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186275480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278079 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ca208624-88d6-5a85-8572-2dd062347b32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278131 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278131 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278131 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278131 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278131 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278131 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278131 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278131 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186277536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278131 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e7b5f25c-b535-59ae-8da4-9392f8bb667d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278141 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278141 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278141 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278141 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278141 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278141 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278141 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278141 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186275668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278141 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ed331e7d-c8f9-522c-8244-24e655efebee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278495 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278495 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161358" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278495 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278495 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,-y,\\,2x⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=3x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 5$ and $-3\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278495 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0bf481ef-95d3-5b3f-b324-29ecd57febda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278495 #edb/ref 1074 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,3u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 5,\\,-3\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,-y,\\,2x⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=3u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨3u-2v,\\,-v,\\,2u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3u-2v,\\,-v,\\,2u⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(3u-2v)\\cdot (-3)+(-v)\\cdot (2)+2u\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-9u+6v-2v+2u \\\\  & =-7u+4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,-y,\\,2x⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-7u+4v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(-7u+4v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278515 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278515 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161453" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278515 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278515 #edb/ref 1071 "For a surface $S$ given by $y=-{x}^{2}z$ for $(x,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,xz+Q+\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?\n\n*Hint: The orientation of $S$ should be chosen such that the unit normal vector has a positive  $j$-component.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278515 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ce5730b3-fc65-5b4c-bdd5-95a34bf939c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278515 #edb/ref 1074 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $y=-{x}^{2}z,$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,z)=⟨x,\\,-{x}^{2}z,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,-2xz,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,-{x}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2xz & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{x}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨-2xz,\\,-1,\\,-{x}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, notice that the $j$-component is negative. Therefore, we select the normal vector that points in the *opposite* direction:\n\n$$\n{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{x}^{′}=-{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′}=⟨2xz,\\,1,\\,{x}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,z))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,R\\,⟩\\cdot ⟨2xz,\\,1,\\,{x}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2P\\,xz+Q+R\\,{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278516 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278516 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161456" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278516 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278516 #edb/ref 1071 "For a surface $S$ given by $x=2yz$ for $(y,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(P+\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,z+\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278516 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a6603224-9e78-54fd-8272-af20dda792ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278516 #edb/ref 1074 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $x=2yz,$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(y,z)=⟨2yz,\\,y,\\,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨2z,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨2y,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2z & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2y & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨1,\\,-2z,\\,-2y⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(y,z))\\cdot ({r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-2z,\\,-2y⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(P+(\\,-2Q)\\,z+(\\,-2R)\\,y\\,)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278518 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278518 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161462" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278518 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278518 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=y-x$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278518 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "06f1e075-9f39-52f0-b9b8-c179d2533ffc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278518 #edb/ref 1074 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,v-u⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=v-u} \\\\  & =⟨v-u,\\,v+2(v-u),\\,2u-v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v-u,\\,3v-2u,\\,2u-v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨v-u,\\,3v-2u,\\,2u-v⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(v-u)\\cdot 1+(3v-2u)\\cdot (-1)+(2u-v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =v-u-3v+2u+2u-v \\\\  & =3u-3v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3u-3v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(3u-3v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278547 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278547 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161541" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278547 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278547 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,{z}^{2}+1⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=2\\sqrt{xy}$ for $3\\le x\\le 4$ and $1\\le y\\le 2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278547 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1788e522-3caf-5313-8725-17c2fd98bec0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278547 #edb/ref 1074 "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\sqrt{xy})=\\sqrt{\\frac{y}{x}} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\sqrt{xy})=\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,{z}^{2}+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,{z}^{2}+1⟩{|}_{z=2\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\  & =⟨{{\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{4xy+1}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}},\\,{z}^{2}+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{y}{x}}-\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}+4xy+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1-\\frac{x}{y}+4xy+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-\\frac{x}{y}+4xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(-\\frac{x}{y}+4xy)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}{[-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+2x{y}^{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+8x+0-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2){[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7(6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373965 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373965 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161381" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373965 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373965 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z+x,\\,y+2z,\\,x-4y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2x-4y$ for $-2\\le x\\le 0$ and $-1\\le y\\le 5.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{5}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373965 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "acc5680d-481f-574e-9c37-7723114fd2f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373965 #edb/ref 1074 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2u-4v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 0,\\,-1\\le v\\le 5\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z+x,\\,y+2z,\\,x-4y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2u-4v} \\\\  & =⟨2u-4v+u,\\,v+2(2u-4v),\\,u-4v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3u-4v,\\,4u-7v,\\,u-4v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3u-4v,\\,4u-7v,\\,u-4v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,4,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(3u-4v)\\cdot (-2)+(4u-7v)\\cdot 4+(u-4v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-6u+8v+16u-28v+u-4v \\\\  & =11u-24v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z+x,\\,y+2z,\\,x-4y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(11u-24v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{5}(11u-24v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373966 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373966 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373966 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373966 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921