1\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373972 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9a86f1df-9194-5ee6-ac19-2bfbeca02663" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373972 #edb/ref 1074 "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-2x)=-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-2x)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,z+2x⟩{|}_{z=y-2x} \\\\  & =⟨y,\\,x+(y-2x),\\,y-2x+2x⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{y-x}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{y}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,z+2x⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y\\cdot (-2)-(y-x)\\cdot (1)+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2y-y+x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2y+x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2y+x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[{y}^{2}+xy]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(1+x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2+2-1-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373973 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373973 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373975 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373973 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373973 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373973 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373973 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373973 #edb/